+# After-task: t9 profile coverage, G=30 sigma slope and sd_g=0.1 (#1562)
+
+Shannon / Fisher. No code change to `R/` or `src/`. No C17 recertify.
+No subagents.
+
+## 1. Goal
+
+Lane t9 (receipt `sweep-oct16/t9`, pin `ca3ddefa`) reported two profile
+cells outside the [93%, 97%] bar. The task was to investigate the G=30
+sigma-slope miss and fix it **if it is a bug**.
+
+## 2. Finding: not a profile-construction bug
+
+### Sigma slope at G=30, sd_g=0.5 — 90.3%
+
+From `sweep-oct16/t9/results/coverage_summary.tsv` (300 reps):
+
+| engine | method | n_cover / n_attempt | coverage |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| drmTMB | profile `fixef:sigma:x` | 271 / 300 | 0.9033 |
+| drmTMB | Wald `fixef:sigma:x` | 271 / 300 | 0.9033 |
+| drmTMB | bootstrap `fixef:sigma:x` | 90 / 100 | 0.9000 |
+| DRModels.jl | profile `sigma_slope` | 280 / 300 | 0.9333 (in bar) |
+| DRModels.jl | Wald `sigma_slope` | 280 / 300 | 0.9333 |
+
+Wald and profile miss **exactly the same 29/300** on drmTMB. That is the
+signature of a finite-sample MLE location, not a broken LR root-finder:
+the profile is tracking the same likelihood as the Hessian. The issue's
+example seed `20261017814` has profile interval ≈ `[0.379, 0.669]`
+entirely above the true slope 0.3 — an upward-biased point, not an
+asymmetric or truncated profile.
+
+Julia on the same DGP is inside the pass bar (93.3%). The 3 pp R–Julia
+gap is an estimator difference (TMB ML vs Woodbury), not evidence that
+`profile_endpoint_crossing` dropped a root.
+
+MCSE of a 90.3% binomial at n=300 is 1.7 pp; 90.3% sits about 2.7
+nominal SE below 95%. That is a real small-sample miss, shared with
+Wald.
+
+### sd_g overcover at true sd_g=0.1
+
+| cell | G | coverage | `profile.boundary` |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 | 10 | 0.9733 | 287 / 300 |
+| 3 | 30 | 0.9833 | 282 / 300 |
+
+This is the intended Self–Liang / `[0, u]` behaviour
+(`allow_lower_boundary = TRUE` for `exp` targets in
+`profile_endpoint_crossing`). A one-sided interval that includes 0
+covers a small positive truth more often than 95%. Not a bug. The twin
+Julia defect (throw / `(-Inf, Inf)` instead of `[0, u]`) is DRModels.jl
+#1117.
+
+Wald `sd:mu:(1 | g)` at the same cells (0.36 / 0.42 with many Inf) is
+already opened as Refs #1558. Bootstrap sigma-intercept undercover
+(0.87–0.91 in 3/4 cells) is Refs #1315.
+
+## 3a. Options if the slope miss must be closed (not chosen)
+
+1. **Document only.** `?confint.drmTMB` already warns that profile
+   coverage at a variance boundary is not calibrated. A sentence that
+   the *sigma slope* at G≈30 with a non-negligible mean RE can run ~5 pp
+   low, matching Wald, would match the t9 number without changing the
+   interval.
+2. **Small-sample df for scale coefficients.** #1558 / #680 machinery
+   currently does not reach `fixef:sigma:*`. Extending `small_sample_df`
+   to the residual-scale slope is a methods choice (which df?).
+3. **Bias-correct the sigma-slope MLE** (Firth / JE). Out of scope; the
+   profile is not the broken piece.
+4. **Do nothing.** Julia's 93.3% on the same DGP is in bar; the R miss
+   is the TMB point, not the CI constructor.
+
+FX5 rules: stop on a methods choice. No `R/profile.R` edit.
+
+## 4. Files touched
+
+This note only. `R/`, `src/`, and `tests/` are unchanged, so C17 is not
+re-run.
+
+## 5. Checks
+
+Coverage arithmetic is from the committed t9 summary (300 + 300 + 100
+reps, zero silent NaN). No new simulation was run. The example seed was
+not re-fit in this session (R/TMB not installed in the agent image).
